{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1498903-a-thousand-venoms","id":1498903,"title":"A Thousand Venoms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-12-05T18:13:05-08:00","id":1498903,"title":"A Thousand Venoms","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Even back in the grandish old days of First Edition, I've long felt an odd attachment to the Venombite kith. Something about their thematics, their mythos, their personal struggles struck a secret chord on my heartstrings. They are near; they are dear. I think about my precious Winter Courtier neurasthenic violinist named Fiddleback from years and years ago, and I blink and I smile. With Kith &amp; Kin we now have an official 2e update, which has left me with a frothy affogato of ideas that I jotted down today at work during my ample downtime. It's a system for customization, fine-tuning the agony your character can inflict to better reflect your own personal story. So, ah, here it is!</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Just as a neurotoxin and a hemotoxin destroy in unique ways, two different Venombites can possess widely divergent poisons. Fae toxicology is a staggeringly complex field that nevertheless boils down to one simple principle: Assumptions are as deadly as a blue-ringed octopus. One Venombite's injection might give you just a few hours to live unless you can drag yourself to the freehold's sole Asclepian in time, while another leaves you in a state of sickly-sweet delirium after a tender kiss under eerie stars. The Strangers are no strangers to the myriad venoms that steep in the hearts of man, after all.<br /> <br /> <b>Systems</b><br /> <br /> At character creation, a player can customize the effects of their Venombite's Trickery, deconstructing the base effect and building it back up in different ways. For reference, a &quot;standard&quot; Venombite can, once per scene, enhance a normal Brawl attack with a point of Glamour to inflict lethal damage and levy the grave Poisoned Tilt on the victim. This system gives the player a set of points to trade for differing effects. The &quot;standard&quot; Venombite has all its points preset. Consult the chart below for costs and adjustments:<ul><li>Attack inflicts a moderate Personal Tilt: 1 Point</li> <li>Attack inflicts a severe Personal Tilt: 2 Points</li> <li>Attack only inflicts bashing damage: +1 Point</li> <li>Attack inflicts no damage: +2 Points</li> <li>Attack requires use of a grapple move or otherwise intimate contact: +1 Point</li> </ul>This means as well that the player can downgrade the Venombite's Poisoned Tilt to moderate to recoup one point, or obviate it entirely for two. The Storyteller may rule that not all Personal Tilts are appropriate for the kith Trickery. Flesh Too Solid cannot be chosen as an effect for this Trickery. For the purposes of the Immobilized Tilt, the poison has an effective Durability equal to (Wyrd/2, round down).<br /> <br /> NB: This hack uses the more comprehensive/systematized rules for Tilts found in Deviant: The Renegades. Refer to that book for more information on the distinction between moderate and severe Tilts.<br /> <br /> At Storyteller discretion, a Venombite might be able to alter the effects of their personal poison while within the mutable space of the Hedge. This requires a Paradigm Shift with successes equal to (5 + total points shifted). High-Wyrd Venombites may be able to develop even more potent venoms, or ones whose effects are more esoteric than anything a rattlesnake or sea wasp could produce.<br /> <br /> Additionally, some Venombites display a different kith Blessing from the norm: When the changeling makes an Intimidate roll to deter an aggressor (or someone they believe to be such), three successes counts as an exceptional success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-06T09:16:35-08:00","id":1498963,"title":"","content":"Could I do something like this? Do the tilts last for a scene?<br /> <br /> Standard: Grave Poisoned, Lethal Damage<br /> +2 Points (attack inflicts no damage)<br /> +2 Points (attack doesn't inflicted Poisoned)<br /> -2 Points (attack inflicts Severe Arm Wrack)<br /> -2 Points (attack inflicts Severe Leg Wrack)<br /> New: Severe Arm Wrack, Severe Leg Wrack, No Damage<br /> <br /> Weston is a Venombite Changeling from a Keeper called &quot;The Stockades,&quot; who put people in cruel medieval punishments, restraining and torturing people to their limits. With a simple touch of his hand, his enemies are put back in the same position he was put in for all those years, arms and legs broken and busted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Proud creator of <b><a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/420206/Curiouser-and-Curiouser-Bargains\" target=\"_blank\">Curiouser and Curiouser Bargains</a></b>, a collection of 30+ Homebrew Contracts and 10+ Entitlements on the STV!<br /> My <b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GFE19F9st7dhGh9zv_hEQyOSm80Xp7dQwmvFg2SAXJY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules</a></b> for Changeling!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17SsOsKpfdANVZscFHSO_afTx-gD3h0iX3p5q07V4u50/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Vampire!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kR6ASTLjaEDwl3zgANnkRrbk0-s2bvw40uXwS-q15O0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Geist!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27667-super-vlad","name":"Super Vlad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27667_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-06T19:19:23-08:00","id":1499012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Super Vlad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1498903-a-thousand-venoms?p=1498963#post1498963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could I do something like this? Do the tilts last for a scene?<br /> <br /> Standard: Grave Poisoned, Lethal Damage<br /> +2 Points (attack inflicts no damage)<br /> +2 Points (attack doesn't inflicted Poisoned)<br /> -2 Points (attack inflicts Severe Arm Wrack)<br /> -2 Points (attack inflicts Severe Leg Wrack)<br /> New: Severe Arm Wrack, Severe Leg Wrack, No Damage<br /> <br /> Weston is a Venombite Changeling from a Keeper called &quot;The Stockades,&quot; who put people in cruel medieval punishments, restraining and torturing people to their limits. With a simple touch of his hand, his enemies are put back in the same position he was put in for all those years, arms and legs broken and busted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that works perfectly. Normally each Tilt has a specific way of ending it, although a number do fade at the end of the scene. Arm and Leg Wrack are specifically tied to damage in their normal forms, so I would probably as well have them end with the scene if no actual damage is involved.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}